WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.749
What to carry into the next lesson.

2
00:00:02.029 --> 00:00:03.139
Five ideas.

3
00:00:03.419 --> 00:00:11.675
A protocol turns N-by-M integrations into N plus M, which matters once several AI applications need the same systems.

4
00:00:11.955 --> 00:00:18.995
The host owns the conversation and runs one client per server; servers are isolated from each other by design.

5
00:00:19.275 --> 00:00:25.888
Tools are the model’s choice, resources the application’s, prompts the user’s, and that tells you where to put review.

6
00:00:26.168 --> 00:00:30.755
The current revision is stateless and asks the user for input through elicitation.

7
00:00:31.035 --> 00:00:37.093
And stdio is for servers that need your machine, Streamable HTTP for shared services.

8
00:00:37.373 --> 00:00:38.888
Next, you build a server.
